## Step-by-step Instructions

1. Read the vulnerability description to determine the most suitable base commit:
   - Currently, the base commit of the repository is `{{ base_commit }}`
   - If you identify a more suitable base commit based on the description:
     a. Save the commit hash to `/testcase/base_commit_hash`
     b. Switch to this commit using `git reset --hard <commit_hash>`
   - Otherwise, use the provided `{{ base_commit }}` as the base commit:
     a. Save it to `/testcase/base_commit_hash`
   - Note that `/testcase/base_commit_hash` FILE SHOULD BE CREATED before moving to the next step.

2. Run {% if container_id %}`docker exec {{ container_id }} bash -c "cd {{ work_dir }} && secb build"`{% else %}`cd {{ work_dir }} && secb build`{% endif %} to build the project.

3. Improve the build script (`/src/build.sh`):
   a. Make it standalone - remove undefined variables
   b. Remove fuzzer-related build commands
   c. Add `-j$(nproc)` to make commands
   d. Add `-p` to mkdir commands
   e. Keep only essential build commands
   f. Preserve existing compiler flags when adding new ones
   g. Add script existence checks before running local scripts (e.g., ./autogen.sh)
   h. Place `make clean` before configure/make commands
   i. `$SRC` and `$WORK` are predefined as `/src` and `/work`

4. Build using {% if container_id %}`docker exec {{ container_id }} bash -c "cd {{ work_dir }} && secb build"`{% else %}`cd {{ work_dir }} && secb build`{% endif %}

5. If build errors occur:
   - Focus on `error` messages only (ignore warnings)
   - Add suppression flags before configure command
   - Make MINIMAL source code changes if necessary

6. Record installed packages in `/testcase/packages.txt` (one per line, if any)

7. Save source changes:
   {% if container_id %}`docker exec {{ container_id }} bash -c "cd {{ work_dir }} && git diff --no-color {{ base_commit }} > /testcase/repo_changes.diff"`{% else %}`cd {{ work_dir }} && git diff --no-color {{ base_commit }} > /testcase/repo_changes.diff`{% endif %}

8. Verify deliverables exist:
   - `/testcase/base_commit_hash`
   - `/testcase/repo_changes.diff`
   - `/testcase/packages.txt` (if packages installed)
   - `/src/build.sh`

## Troubleshooting
- C++17 errors: add `-std=c++14` to CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS
- Implicit int errors: add explicit type declarations
- Function overload errors: add `-D_GNU_SOURCE`

## Notes
- DO NOT disable sanitizer options
- Use `secb build` to prevent long output logs
- Limit command output with `head` when needed
